## http_serve_supervised end-to-end smoke — D.11 Phase 2 chunk 2c.
##
## Passive smoke: binds the supervised server on :18737 and waits for
## SIGTERM/SIGINT. Verified end-to-end with external `curl` (see the
## verification recipe below).
##
## Why passive (no in-process request driver): under the current
## scheduler model, `sched_spawn(async fn())` inline-polls the spawned
## function up to its first true suspension point. A driver goroutine
## that does `usleep(...)` blocks the spawning thread until the usleep
## completes — main thread can't enter http_serve_supervised in
## parallel; the listener loop never runs; the driver's requests get
## connection-refused. Proved by adding diagnostic prints —
## `connect()` returned -1 every iteration; the bind never happened.
## True multi-thread M:N concurrency for the driver pattern is filed
## for Phase 2d when http_request_selectable lands (the per-conn loop
## will use unified select on request-read which yields properly to
## other goroutines).
##
## Build:
##   ./self-hosted/bin/quartz spec/qz/http_serve_supervised_smoke.qz \
##     | llc -filetype=obj -o /tmp/hss.o
##   clang /tmp/hss.o -o /tmp/hss -lm -lpthread \
##     -L/opt/homebrew/opt/openssl@3/lib -lssl -lcrypto
##
## Verify (in one shell):
##   /tmp/hss
##
## In another shell:
##   curl -sv http://127.0.0.1:18737/
##   # → HTTP/1.1 200 OK / Content-Type: text/plain / "ok-from-supervised"
##   curl -X POST -d 'hello' http://127.0.0.1:18737/echo
##   # → 200 / "ok-from-supervised"
##
## Then SIGTERM the first shell (Ctrl+C or `kill -TERM <pid>`); the
## listener loop's top-of-iteration poll observes _http_shutdown_flag
## (set by signal_on_flag), drains in-flight connections via
## http_dyn_gsup_stop, and returns 0 when connection tasks cooperate. A truly
## held blocked connection currently requires the parked runtime cancellation
## fix documented in the conductor ledger.
##
## Verified 2026-05-23 — 3 sequential curl requests all returned 200
## with body "ok-from-supervised"; SIGTERM-driven shutdown clean.

import * from std/net/http_server

def smoke_handler(req: Request): Response
  return text_response("ok-from-supervised")
end

def main(): Int
  puts("http_serve_supervised — D.11 Phase 2 chunk 2c smoke")
  puts("Listening on :18737 — curl in another shell, then SIGTERM (Ctrl+C)")
  var config = http_server_config(18737)
  config.max_connections = 1
  config.shutdown_timeout_ms = 100
  return http_serve_supervised(config, smoke_handler)
end
